@bank all old
// The lines section 20 had hard-coded before 0.43.0 (CHAT_GREET, CHAT_NEAR, CHAT_LIFE, CHAT_DEPT, CHATTER_IDLE),
// moved here unchanged. "old" marks them so section 20 keeps picking them exactly as before until it asks lineFor.
// Keep their order: the old picking counts on it. New shared lines go in other bank files.

== greet
? tier=stranger
- Oh, hello.
- Hi.
- Can I help you?
- Morning. Or is it evening? I lose track.
- You're the new Works cadet, aren't you?
- Hello there.
- Mm? Oh, hi.
- Don't think we've met.
- Afternoon.
- All right?
? tier=acquaintance
- Hey, {me}.
- Oh, hi again.
- Hello, cadet.
- Good to see you.
- How's Works treating you?
- Hi! Settling in?
- You again! Hi.
- Hey. Busy day?
- Hello, hello.
- Nice to see a familiar face.
? tier=colleague
- {me}! Just who I wanted to see.
- Hey, how's it going?
- There you are.
- Good timing, I could use a break.
- Hi, {me}. Keeping out of trouble?
- Oh good, it's you.
- Hey, colleague.
- How's your day been?
- Pull up a chair.
- Hi! Got a minute?
? tier=friend
- {me}! Come here, you.
- Hey, friend.
- Was hoping I'd run into you.
- There's my favourite cadet.
- You look like you need a tea.
- Hey! Sit, sit.
- Oh, I'm glad you're here.
- Just the person.
- How are you really?
- Hi! Tell me everything.
? tier=close
- {me}! Best part of my day.
- Hey, you.
- I saved you a seat. Well, I would have.
- There you are, I was about to come looking.
- My favourite person aboard.
- Hey! I've got so much to tell you.
- Oh, thank the stars, a friendly face.
- Hi, {me}. Missed you.
- Come on, walk with me.
- You always turn up at the right time.

== near
? act:work
- Busy shift in the {room}.
- Never a quiet minute in the {room}.
- Can't stop long. Work.
- The {room} keeps me on my toes.
- Halfway through the shift. Nearly there.
? act:breakfast|dinner
- The food's good today.
- Brennan's outdone herself.
- I was starving.
- Best part of the day, this.
- Mind if I eat while we talk?
? act:gym
- Just warming up.
- Don't mind me, I'm all sweat.
- Trying to beat yesterday.
- Gym's busy tonight.
? act:wash
- Not the best time for a chat, is it?
- Give me a minute to dry off.
?
- Nice and quiet in the {room} right now.
- I like it here in the {room}.
- Just taking it easy.
- Needed a moment to myself.
- This is my favourite spot.

== life
? habit:early-riser
- Up before the lights, me. Always have been.
? habit:late-sleeper
- Don't talk to me before my second tea.
? habit:night-owl
- I do my best thinking after midnight.
? habit:early-to-bed
- I'll be asleep by nine. No shame.
? habit:skips-breakfast
- Breakfast? Never had the habit.
? habit:late-diner
- I always end up eating last.
? habit:lingers-at-meals
- I could sit over dinner for hours.
? habit:window-seat
- I always grab a window seat. The stars never get old.
? habit:workaholic
- I'll stay late again tonight, probably.
? habit:tea-break
- My mid-shift tea is sacred.
? habit:gym-regular
- Gym after shift keeps me sane.
? habit:garden-lover
- You should see the tomatoes in the garden.
? habit:lounge-regular
- Come by the bow lounge some evening.
? habit:quiet-corner
- I know all the quiet corners on this ship.
? habit:common-room
- The common room's the best place on the ship.
? habit:music
- I like to sit in the music room after shift.
? habit:calls-home
- Called home yesterday. Everyone's well.
? habit:evening-shower
- An evening shower and I sleep like a stone.
? habit:runner
- I'm trying to beat my lap time on the treadmill.
? habit:shopper
- The store had new tea in. I bought too much.
? habit:musician
- I've been learning a new piece. Badly.
? habit:gardener
- The herbs in the garden are coming on nicely.
? habit:bar-regular
- One drink in the lounge after dinner. Tradition.
? habit:stargazer
- The observatory's amazing at night. You should come up.
? dept:command
- The bridge is calmer than people think.
? dept:helm
- Steady as she goes, on my watch.
? dept:comms
- You wouldn't believe the static we pick up.
? dept:works
- Something always needs fixing, doesn't it?
? dept:watch
- Quiet watch so far. I like it that way.
? dept:survey
- Sato has us chasing another reading.
? dept:infirmary
- Drink some water. Doctor's orders. Well, aide's orders.
? dept:galley
- Two hundred meals a day, and they still ask what's for dinner.

== smalltalk
? act:meal
- Pass the salt?
- Is this the new recipe?
- I'm stuffed.
- Brennan's outdone herself.
- Seconds? Go on then.
- Who made the bread?
? act:work
- Hand me that, would you?
- Nearly done here.
- Who logged this one?
- Check that again for me.
- Right, next.
? act:free
- Did you see the stars last night?
- I could sit here all evening.
- Long day.
- Fancy a game later?
- Heard from home lately?
- Ha! No way.
